# api/

`api/openapi.yaml` lives here: the authoritative transport contract for this
application's JSON API. It is hand-edited, and both the Go server bindings
(`internal/platform/httpapi/openapigen/`) and the TypeScript models
(`frontend/src/lib/api/schema.d.ts`) are generated from it.

This directory has no OpenAPI document yet. Later API tasks add the contract,
generated bindings, and typed frontend client. The routing boundary already
exists in `internal/platform/httpapi/router.go`: register operation routes
relative to `/api/v1` through `httpapi.Deps.RegisterAPI`. Unknown paths under
that exact prefix remain API `404` responses and never fall through to the
embedded frontend.

The API and document routers are sibling security boundaries with independent
policies. Application middleware may be added only through the documented
`httpapi.MiddlewareSlots`, inside the fixed security, request identity/logging,
recovery, and metrics core. Keep `router_test.go` current if the application
deliberately changes that contract.
